# Build-time settings for the browser end-to-end build (`vite build --mode e2e`).
#
# The suite runs headless, where WebGL falls back to software rasterization and every per-pixel
# term is paid in CPU instead of by a GPU. Multisampling is one such term, so it is off here.
#
# No assertion in the suite inspects edge quality; the specs read the stage through its debug
# attributes, never its pixels. Turning it off therefore costs no coverage.
#
# It is a reduction, not a remedy. A software-rasterizing host still spends whole cores per canvas
# with this off, because the frame is re-rasterized every ticker tick whether or not the scene
# changed. Do not read a green suite here as evidence that canvases have become cheap.
VITE_SC_ANTIALIAS=0
